 hypertension (197/128 mmHg)", "Tachycardia (100/min)", "Hypoxia (95% saturation)", "Chronic metabolic risk factors (diabetes, dyslipidemia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Mechanical Bowel Obstruction or Adhesion-related Intestinal Dysfunction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.24418604651162798, "posterior": 0.33220338983050846, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The RLQ scar and abdominal findings are more consistent with adhesion-related mechanical dysfunction than diabetes-related motility disorders, though the subac…"], "evidence_against": ["Adhesions typically present acutely or intermittently, so a 7-day subacute course weakens this diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Diabetes-related Gastrointestinal Motility Disorders", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.1744186046511628, "posterior": 0.20338983050847453, "danger": 0.45, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The diabetes-fatty meal-vomiting link supports gastroparesis, but abdominal findings like the RLQ scar and tympanitic abdomen make it less likely."], "evidence_against": ["The RLQ scar is more consistent with mechanical dysfunction, indirectly reducing the likelihood of diabetes-related motility disorders."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "risk_context", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Constipation with Complications", "parent": "ROO